--TEST--
an enum case renamed at its declaration is renamed as a key inside a class constant table, as a key of a keyed literal and in a subscript, and the other cases are left alone, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`, `rule:types/arrays`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Priority { Low, Normal, Hi<|>gh }

final class Labels
{
    const array<Priority, string> LABELS = [Priority::Low => 'low', Priority::High => 'high'];
}

array<Priority, string> $short = [Priority::High => 'h', Priority::Low => 'l'];
echo $short[Priority::High];
--REQUEST--
rename to=Urgent
--EXPECT--
case.nvs:2:30 Urgent
case.nvs:6:78 Urgent
case.nvs:9:45 Urgent
case.nvs:10:23 Urgent
